# Project Rules

## Language

- **Code stays English.** All code, identifiers, file names, comments, commit
  messages, and assistant responses MUST be in English.
- **Site content is multilingual.** User-facing content may be localized into
  the supported locales: English (`en`, canonical source), Danish (`da`),
  German (`de`), and Swedish (`sv`). English is the source of truth; the other
  locales are translated from it.
- URL slugs are English by default; localized slugs are allowed only via the
  slug-pair mechanism in `src/data/lang.ts`.
- Product and brand names (the RoomAlyzer lines and product names) are NOT
  translated — they stay identical across all locales, with **one approved
  exceptions** in German (`de`): "Water detector" → **"Wasserdetektor"**;
  "Outdoor" → **"Außen Sensor"**. Per-locale name overrides live in
  `src/data/sensorCategories.ts` (`localizedSensorName`); do not add others
  without explicit approval.
- When adding new content, write the English version first, then provide the
  translations (or rely on the English fallback) for the other locales.

### English copy style (`en`)

English user-facing copy uses **British English** and **sentence case**:

| Rule | Do | Don't |
|------|----|-------|
| **Spelling** | `optimise`, `licence` (noun), `centre`, `defence`, `utilisation`, `organised`, `anonymised` | American `-ize`, `-or` where `-ise`/`-our` is standard |
| **Capitalisation** | Capitalise only the first word and proper nouns/acronyms | Title Case on multi-word headings |
| **Product names** | Keep RoomAlyzer lines and catalogue names unchanged | Translate or re-case product names |
| **Plan tiers** | Single-word tier names stay as-is: `Building`, `Portfolio`, `Enterprise` | — |
| **URL slugs** | English slugs unchanged (`trust-center`, etc.) | Rename routes for spelling |

### Localization grammar (`da`, `de`, `sv`)

Non-English locales follow locale-specific grammar in addition to the product-name
rules below. Use `localizedSensorName()` and `formatProductLabel()` in
`src/data/sensorCategories.ts` for product display names.

| Locale | Rule | Do | Don't |
|--------|------|----|-------|
| **German (`de`)** | Standard noun capitalization | `Sensor`, `Sensoren`, `Entscheidungen`, `Open/Close Sensor` | Lowercase nouns (`sensor`, `entscheidungen`) |
| **German (`de`)** | Product display names | English catalogue token + capitalized suffix (`Humidity Sensor`); approved overrides (`Wasserdetektor`, `Außen Sensor`) everywhere on `/de/` | `Outdoor Sensor`, `Open/Close sensor` |
| **Danish / Swedish (`da` / `sv`)** | Sentence case (mirror `en`) | `sensor`, `sensorer`; hyphenated compounds (`Humidity-sensoren`, `CO2-sensor`) | English Title Case (`CO2 Sensor`, `Temperature Sensor`) |
| **Danish / Swedish (`da` / `sv`)** | Product suffixes in prose | `Humidity-sensoren`, `CO2-sensorn` | `Humidity sensoren` (space before Scandinavian suffix) |

### Em dashes (`en`, `da`, `de`, `sv`)

Use em dashes (—) sparingly in **all locales**. At most **one em dash per
sentence**; at most **two per paragraph**, and only when sentences are short
and distinct. Stacking 2–3 dashes in one sentence or paragraph reads heavy on
the page.

| Rule | Do | Don't |
|------|----|-------|
| **Density** | One dash per sentence where it clearly adds emphasis or contrast | Paired asides (`— X —`), list-in-dash patterns, or 2–3 dashes in one sentence |
| **Paired asides** | Commas, parentheses, or a sentence split | `when you order — Air, Space, or Water — you get…` |
| **Lists in dashes** | Commas or parentheses: `(baseline, measure, analyse, remediate, verify)` | `baseline — measure, analyse — verify` |
| **Product labels** | Colon: `RoomAlyzer Air: indoor climate` | `RoomAlyzer Air — indoor climate` |
| **Product names** | Keep RoomAlyzer line and product names unchanged | Translate or re-case product names |
| **Translations** | Mirror the reduced dash count; use locale-appropriate punctuation | Literal dash-for-dash copy from English |

**Keep a single dash when it works:** a strong aside, contrast, or label where
commas or parentheses read worse. One dash in an SEO `<title>` separator is
fine if it is the only dash in that field (e.g. `Articles — every guide | …`).

**Prefer instead of a second dash:** commas, parentheses, colons, or splitting
into two sentences.

**Examples (English):**

| Before | After |
|--------|-------|
| `when you order — Air, Space, or Water — you get everything` | `when you order RoomAlyzer Air, Space, or Water, you get everything` |
| `measures — PI/TWPI, mould risk, EN 15757 — for museums` | `measures (PI/TWPI, mould risk, EN 15757) for museums` |
| `before a battery runs flat — not after — so you can plan` | `before a battery runs flat, not after, so you can plan` |
| `The teams that champion — and approve — space decisions` | `The teams that champion and approve space decisions` |

**Out of scope:** UI/data glyphs (e.g. `"—"` as a compare-table “no value”
marker), code comments, and JSDoc unless they render on the public site.

### Localization content rules (names, places, standards)

When translating or localizing copy (`da` / `de` / `sv`), follow these rules
in addition to the product-name rules above:

| Category | Rule |
|----------|------|
| **Person names** | Never translate (team, quotes, bylines). |
| **Customer org / brand names** | Use the **official registered name** (e.g. `Erzdiözese Freiburg`, `Evangelische Kirche in Hessen und Nassau`, `Dansk Industri`, `Sweco`). Do not paraphrase into another language. |
| **Danish municipalities (customers)** | Use **locale-appropriate government label + place name**: `Varde Kommune` (da), `Gemeinde Varde` (de), `Varde kommun` (sv). Keep geographic spelling (`Solrød`, `Holbæk`). No erroneous possessives (e.g. not `Gribskovs kommun`). |
| **Geographic proper nouns** | Keep official spelling (`Freiburg`, `Roskilde`, `Hessen`). |
| **Standards and acronyms** | Keep the **official identifier** unchanged: `EN 15757`, `GDPR`, `CO₂`, `ISO 27001`, `MQTT`, `BR18`, `DGNB`, etc. Translate only the explanatory prose around them. |
| **Locale-specific regulations** | May name local rules (`BR18`, `APV`, `EHF`/`PEPPOL`) but on non-DK locales add jurisdiction context or “or your local equivalent” where relevant. |
| **Glossary terms** | Keep `term` and `anchor` as canonical identifiers; translate `short` and `detail` only. |
| **Sensor `heroTitle`** | Do not add “Sensor”/“sensor” suffixes in i18n overlays; use English catalogue titles + `localizedSensorName()` for approved DE exceptions only. |

## Excluded personnel

- **Dennis Knudsen** must not appear anywhere on this website — team
  pages, contact lists, press material, case studies, blog posts, metadata,
  or generated content. He no longer works at IoT Fabrikken. If his name
  appears in existing content, remove it. Do not add him back unless the
  user explicitly revokes this rule.

## RoomAlyzer product portfolio (official)

The authoritative product list uses **four lines only**. Do not publish Series A/B/C,
vendor names (e.g. Disruptive Technologies, Efento), or other alternate groupings.

| Line | Products |
|------|----------|
| **RoomAlyzer Air** | CO2, Full+, Humidity, Mini+, Mini+ PIR, Outdoor, Temperature |
| **RoomAlyzer Space** | Desk, Motion, Open/Close, Touch |
| **RoomAlyzer Water** | Water detector, Water rope |
| **Miscellaneous** | Cloud connector, Range Extender and Bracket |

- **Full+ PIR** is RoomAlyzer Air but must **not** appear on the site until explicitly approved.
- **When adding a new product**, ask which RoomAlyzer line it belongs to before updating the catalogue.
- Product sheet PDFs are localized. Sources under `Productsheets/{EN,DE,DK}/`;
  served via `scripts/sync-product-sheets.mjs` into:
  - English (canonical): `/downloads/product-sheets/{slug}.pdf`
  - German: `/downloads/product-sheets/de/{slug}.pdf`
  - Danish: `/downloads/product-sheets/da/{slug}.pdf`
  Swedish sheets do not exist yet, so `sv` pages fall back to the English PDF.
  Use `productSheetPath(slug, lang)` (`src/data/sensorCategories.ts`) to resolve
  the correct URL. Re-run the sync script whenever the source PDFs change.
- Catalogue data: [`src/data/hubs/sensors.ts`](src/data/hubs/sensors.ts).

## Events hub and landing pages

Events are **temporary**. Hub cards and landing pages hide after `endDate` +
`EVENT_ARCHIVE_GRACE_DAYS` in [`src/data/events.ts`](src/data/events.ts). Structure and
templates stay permanent — see [`src/data/events/README.md`](src/data/events/README.md)
and [`archive/events/`](archive/events/).

Authoritative registry: [`src/data/events.ts`](src/data/events.ts). Card themes:
[`src/data/eventCardThemes.ts`](src/data/eventCardThemes.ts).

### Live vs template vs archive

| Layer | What persists |
|-------|----------------|
| **Live** | `siteEvents` rows; hub cards; landing + contact pages (only while `isEventLive`) |
| **Template** | [`EventLandingLayout.astro`](src/components/events/EventLandingLayout.astro), `EventCardActive`, themes, project rules |
| **Archive** | [`archive/events/{slug}/`](archive/events/) — snapshots after retirement; no public pages |

Filter helpers: `isEventLive`, `getLiveEvents`, `getEventStaticPaths`. No public
“past events” list — retired fairs disappear from the hub; old URLs 301 to `/events/`.

### Events hub (`/[lang]/events/`)

**Card 1 — active** ([`EventCardActive.astro`](src/components/events/EventCardActive.astro))

- Shown when `event.hostLocale ===` current locale **and** `isEventLive(event)`.
- **One colour theme per fair** (`eventAssets.cardTheme`). Extend
  [`eventCardThemes.ts`](src/data/eventCardThemes.ts) for new palettes.
- **Fixed markup:** status eyebrow (green dot) → logo → title → date/location with
  left border accent → CTA row with arrow (hub only).
- **Logos:** official assets in `eventAssets.logo` (`public/images/events/{slug}/`).
  Presentation is uniform via **`logoPreset`** in [`eventCardLogo.ts`](src/data/eventCardLogo.ts)
  (referenced from [`eventCardThemes.ts`](src/data/eventCardThemes.ts)) — same on hub Card 1
  and landing venue cards. Pick a preset when adding a fair; do not hand-roll shell classes.
  | Preset | Use when |
  |--------|----------|
  | `rectangle` | Default horizontal wordmark (ARCHIVISTICA) |
  | `rectangleLg` | Slightly taller horizontal mark (WORKTECH) |
  | `roundel` | Compact circular seal in a white roundel when a wide rectangle would leave too much empty space |
  | `bleed` | Asset includes its own background — clipped plate on the card gradient (MUTEC) |
- **Status dot:** the eyebrow dot on Card 1 is **always green** (`emerald-400`), regardless of
  fair theme — including next to “Demnächst” on the German hub.
- **Links to our landing page** — every Card 1 event **must** ship a host-locale landing
  page; hub cards always link there (never directly to the official event site).
- **Hover:** `hover:-translate-y-0.5 hover:shadow-2xl` on the card; `reveal` on an outer
  wrapper.

**Card 2 — news** ([`EventCardNews.astro`](src/components/events/EventCardNews.astro))

- Shown on other locale hubs while the event is live; no foreign landing link.

**Hub layout**

- Card 1 grid → **stone divider** → Card 2 stack; both sorted by `startDate`.
- Empty state copy when no live events (`emptyTitle` / `emptyLead` in `i18n/events.ts`).

| Fair | `cardTheme` | Palette |
|------|-------------|---------|
| ARCHIVISTICA | `navy` | navy / coral / sky |
| WORKTECH26 Stockholm | `worktech` | zinc / violet |
| MUTEC | `mutec` | zinc / amber gradient; logo `bleed` |
| DHBV Verbandstag | `dhbv` | forest green; logo `rectangle` (small seal centred in panel) |

### Event landing pages

**Canonical structure:** [`EventLandingLayout.astro`](src/components/events/EventLandingLayout.astro)
(seven named slots: `hero`, `features`, `quote`, `testimonials`, `photos`, `cta`).
Example implementation: [`archivistica.astro`](src/pages/[lang]/events/archivistica.astro).

- **Required** for every Card 1 event: landing + contact in `hostLocale`; use
  `getEventStaticPaths(slug)` in `getStaticPaths`.
- **Colour:** same `cardTheme` on landing (`Hero` `darkTone` + section accents).
- **Venue card:** `EventCardActive` with `static` + `externalHref` from `officialUrl`;
  `allowVisualOverflow`; always links to the **official event site** in a new tab; same
  hover as hub. When stand/booth info is known, pass `booth={{ label, detail }}` on the
  landing venue card — bold themed headline (e.g. “Besuchen Sie uns”) and light detail line
  (e.g. stand number/hall). Omit `booth` until the stand is confirmed.
  Use `venueCardCopyFromHeroMeta(hubCopy, heroMeta)` so the card shows **Termin** and **Ort**
  from landing i18n (not hub card date/location strings).
- **Termin format:** `formatEventTermin()` in [`eventVenueCard.ts`](src/data/eventVenueCard.ts)
  from `siteEvents` dates — single day `DD.MM.YYYY`; range `DD.MM. – DD.MM.YYYY`; optional
  `terminTime` in landing i18n as ` · HH:MM–HH:MM`. Never spell out month names on the card.
- **Hero meta chips:** [`EventHeroMeta.astro`](src/components/events/EventHeroMeta.astro)
  below the venue card on **every** landing page. Build with `buildLandingHeroMeta(slug,
  heroMetaFields)` — three items: date (`Termin` / localized), city (`Ort` / localized), and
  event name (third row, full width). Layout: row 1 = date + city (two columns); row 2 = event
  name (full width). City only — no country on the `Ort` chip.

**Module teasers:** register `moduleTeasers` on `SiteEvent`; use
`getModuleEventTeaser()` — never hardcode fair links on module pages.

### Adding an event

1. `siteEvents` + `eventAssets` (+ theme if new).
2. Hub copy in `i18n/events.ts`.
3. Landing i18n, images, thin pages via `EventLandingLayout`.
4. `detailLocales` includes host locale; redirects via `getEventRedirectMap()`.

### Retiring an event

1. After `endDate + EVENT_ARCHIVE_GRACE_DAYS` (or `status: "archived"`).
2. Add `{ slug, hostLocale }` to `archivedEvents` (301: landing → `/events/`, contact → `/contact/`).
3. Remove hub copy; snapshot to `archive/events/{slug}/`.
4. Verify build: no hub card; old URLs redirect.

Do not invent alternate hero layouts or skip landing sections without approval.

## General

- Keep changes small and focused.
- Prefer Astro and Tailwind best practices.
- Avoid adding dependencies unless necessary.

## Logo carousel (locked)

The customer logo carousel — the `LogoMarquee.astro` component, its
markup, CSS, JavaScript, the customer roster, the per-customer URLs, and
the logo asset files under `public/logos/` — is **frozen** and must not
be modified in any way (size, spacing, speed, colours, hover effect,
animation, drag behaviour, list contents, ordering, links, or assets).

If a future user request would touch any of the above, you MUST first
ask the user to confirm explicitly that they really want to change the
locked carousel before making the edit. Phrase it as a direct yes/no
confirmation, e.g.: "The logo carousel is locked per project rules — are
you sure you want to change it?"

The only exception is **moving the `<LogoMarquee />` invocation up or
down within a page** (i.e. its vertical position relative to other
sections, with no changes to the component itself). Even this exception
requires explicit confirmation from the user before being applied.
